From 6f4179f3d7e266c3d233c41375b55278a6987281 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 12:09:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Staff notation, chord functions, real-instrument sound,
 transport symbols, compact phone layout

notation.js draws each bar's melody on a staff (clef, key signature,
accidentals, beams, flags, dots, rests, ties, triplets) and analyses
chords as roman numerals with secondary dominants. The player loads the
16-bit packs and the recorded alto sax lead from the new engine (pins
moved to jazzband-op1r 23383d7 and jazzbook 9e439b0), with a Band feel
setting for human timing. Play, pause and stop are symbols. The header
is one compact block with the status under the title, the output meter
moves to the mixer, and one scrolling toolbar replaces two rows, so the
chart starts about 90 px from the top on a phone.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MFtnqVmArJUVScHreHoD7y
